Yes — please test. Here's exactly what to do, and what I changed.

**Hard-reload first.** The rebuilt `classes.wasm` is a different binary; a normal refresh can serve the old one from cache. Use `Ctrl+Shift+R` (or clear the site data for `localhost:8080`).

**Delete the test world before creating a new one.** Any world you created with the previous build has region files whose sector headers were written from garbage, so they are permanently corrupt — they'll keep throwing the same errors even with the fix. Remove it from the world list, then create a fresh world.

## What was actually wrong

Not the stubs. On this wasm-gc classlib, `ByteBuffer.allocateDirect(n)` is `Heap.alloc(n)` — a bump allocation out of reused WASM linear memory — so it returns *dirty* bytes, while the JDK guarantees every element is zero. Every other direct buffer in the game writes before it reads, which hid this. `RegionFile`'s 8192-byte header is the single exception:

```java
int var5 = this.file.read(this.header, 0L);
if (var5 != -1) { ...validate offsets... }
```

On a brand-new region file that read returns `-1`, so the validation loop is skipped and the buffer keeps whatever the last allocation left behind. `offsets` then reports every chunk as allocated at a bogus sector, which is precisely your log: `expected 274432` is `67 * 4096` — a leftover sector count — and `read 0` is the empty file, while larger stale sectors overflow `sector * 4096` into `IllegalArgumentException: Negative position`.

The fix is in [RegionFile.java](src/main/java/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/storage/RegionFile.java#L35-L57): a `zeroedHeader()` factory that explicitly zeros all 8192 bytes, so a new file has no offsets at all and the spawn chunks simply aren't there yet instead of "allocated past EOF".

## What I verified

- `:compileJava` reran and the TeaVM jar contains `zeroedHeader`; the full wasm build finished `BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 25m 47s`.
- Stubs re-derived against the new artifact (`rebuild-stubs.sh auto`): the same single failing body `code#46205` (`br_on_cast` type bug), stubbed as `46205:trap`, size-preserving, post-stub sweep `status=clean masked=0`, both gates pass. Final artifact: 21,320,844 bytes, sha1 `5c2ea692…`, and `classes.wasm.teadbg` contains `zeroedHeader`, so the fix is in the shipped binary.
- Headless Chromium boots the rebuilt module cleanly to the profile screen — no `CompileError`, no import errors.

